From: OPD2413 Maintainer <opd2413@local>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ksldapp: guard SIGUSR1 target pid and retire exiting lock process on fast relock

1. Never call kill(pid, SIGUSR1) with pid <= 0 when lockState() != Unlocked.
   If m_lockProcess is not running (processId() == 0), kill(0, SIGUSR1)
   broadcasts SIGUSR1 to the compositor's entire process group, killing
   kwin_wayland_wrapper. Restart the greeter instead unless emergency mode
   is active.
2. Retire any still-exiting QProcess before starting a new greeter, and
   clear per-instance exit flags on lock(), so a grace-time unlock() ->
   solidSuspend()/lock() race never fails with 'Process is already running'
   or leaves Locked state without a greeter.
